{{- $sdk := .Global.AST.MainSDK }}
{{- $noServers := not (and $sdk.Servers $sdk.Servers.HasAbsoluteURL) }}
{{- $sdkClassName := (sanitizeClassName $sdk.Type.Name) -}}
You can setup your SDK to emit debug logs for SDK requests and responses.

You can pass your own logger class directly into your SDK.
```python
from {{ getModuleImport }} import {{$sdkClassName}}
import logging

logging.basicConfig(level=logging.DEBUG)
s = {{$sdkClassName}}({{- if $noServers }}server_url="https://example.com", {{ end }}debug_logger=logging.getLogger("{{ getAbsoluteModuleImport }}"))
```
{{- if .Global.Config.EnvVarPrefix }}

You can also enable a default debug logger by setting an environment variable `{{ templateDebugEnvVar }}` to true.
{{- end }}